Slippy for Photoshop

Design references (no code copied):
- adb-mcp by Mike Chambers (MIT) - https://github.com/mikechambers/adb-mcp
  The split into a local MCP bridge plus a UXP plug-in that dials out to it,
  and batchPlay as the escape hatch.
- PS-MCP-IMT (CC BY-NC 4.0) - ideas only; no code from it is used here.
  Reporting "Photoshop is busy" instead of hanging when Photoshop is modal.

The rules this plug-in follows (one call = one undo, writes run alone, never
save by surprise, no dialogs, one error shape) come from building Slippy for
Adobe Illustrator.
